# ===================================================================
# SimplyBank Ultimate — .gitignore
# Spring Boot 4 / Java 21 / Maven
# ===================================================================

# --- Build output (Maven) ---
target/
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# --- Compiled class files & packaged artifacts ---
*.class
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
# ...but never ignore the Maven wrapper jar (already excepted above)

# --- Secrets & local configuration (CRITICAL — see note below) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local.properties
application-local.properties
application-local.yml
secrets/

# --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log
spring.log

# --- IntelliJ IDEA ---
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/

# --- VS Code ---
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Eclipse / STS ---
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.factorypath
.springBeans

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Claude Code local settings (keep shared config, ignore personal) ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Test & coverage reports ---
.surefire-reports/
jacoco.exec
*.exec

# --- Docker local overrides ---
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- JVM crash dumps ---
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
*.hprof

# ===================================================================
# NOTES
#
# 1) SECRETS: `.env` is ignored, `.env.example` is NOT. The example
#    file (committed) lists the variable NAMES with dummy values so
#    anyone can see what config the app needs; the real `.env` with
#    actual passwords/JWT secret stays on your machine only. This is
#    decision D-secrets from the plan: nothing sensitive in the repo.
#
# 2) MAVEN WRAPPER: `mvnw`, `mvnw.cmd`, and `.mvn/` ARE committed —
#    they let anyone (and the CI runner) build without installing
#    Maven. Only the bulky `target/` build output is ignored.
#
# 3) IDE FILES: ignored entirely. Your IDE config is personal;
#    committing it creates noise in every diff and conflicts between
#    teammates' setups. The project builds from pom.xml alone.
#
# 4) Flyway migrations (src/main/resources/db/migration/) are NOT
#    ignored — they are source code. Mentioned because people
#    sometimes reflexively ignore .sql files. Don't.
# ===================================================================
